I explained in my response Why I was doing What. In case
there's something I forgot to mention, feel free to ask.
I'd be happy to answer any new questions; there's always
the chance of some new insight, as seems to have been the
case with the analysis/response postings.


For the rest of what you wrote I just want to agree to
your remark that I should stop some bad habits. (But you
may imagine how hard that is for that prominent example
of travelling burdened, if from 17 ascensions in the last
year I've done 3 stressed, 14 burdened, and only a single
one unburdened.) There's certainly potential to survive
especially some early/mid game if going permanently (or
temporarily) unburdened, I'm sure, though, there are other
games where it's quite irrelevant because you have powerful
offenses, or effective defenses, or a zoo of killer pets,
and even combinations thereof.

WRT the other decisions named "severe mistakes" (if above
you've meant those "stuff") I just cannot agree, and I
explained why; I could have said even more about the dark
mines issue, for example, but there's nothing new that I
hadn't pointed out already in RGRN during the past years
about that topic, and I assume these factors should be well
known to the attentive audience.

For myself I classified the comments in a couple categories,
for example; bad advice (eating bats), irrelevant (carrying
stones, etc.), disputable choices with strong bias towards
being not preferable *in this case* (pet, mines), and those
suggestions to consider or follow in future games (abstain
from early chest handling in case you have other priorities).
But everyone who read those analysis/response postings shall
make her own decision, depending on own experiences.

As an experienced player you can trade safety measures for
a game play that fits better to your style, taking to some
degree into account that you have to be caucious in certain
situations. Fortunately there are not too many unexpected
events popping in every other level. In some cases you'll
be confronted with accumulations of bad luck, then it may
*or may not* matter that you played suboptimal in a certain
respect. I take the risk of any potential subobtimal detail
in game play to be made responsible for my deaths. (As in
the Caveman vs. soldier ant incident.)

YMMV.

